      <h2>Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>21st Century Jurist Law Review</strong> is a student-led legal publication platform
        dedicated to promoting legal education, critical thinking, and academic writing within South African law
        and global legal systems.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to create a space where law students and aspiring jurists can express ideas,
        publish legal analysis, and engage with real legal issues affecting society today.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Vision</h2>
      <p>
        To become a respected student legal journal that develops future legal minds and contributes
        meaningfully to discussions on justice, rights, and constitutional development.
      </p>

    </div>
